      "root_cause": "Commit 5b0bb55c90 in v1.4.8 raised the default DB_POOL_SIZE from 20 to 100. With 5 API instances, PayStream can open 500 PostgreSQL connections against max_connections of 100, so new connections are refused and POST /payments fails with 500 after the 5 s pool timeout.",
      "summary": "**Root cause:** commit 5b0bb55c90 in v1.4.8 raised the default `DB_POOL_SIZE` from 20 to 100 [F3][F4]. Each of the 5 instances keeps its own pool, so PayStream can now open 500 connections, five times Postgres' `max_connections` of 100 [F5][I1].\n\nThe errors began during the v1.4.8 rollout and hit every instance [F2][F7][I2]: 94 `POST /payments` requests failed with `OperationalError: too many connections` after waiting 5 s for a pool slot [F1]. INC-017 had the same cause at a smaller scale, a pool of 60 [F6][I3].\n\nThe first error came 6 minutes into the rollout [F8]. That fits pools that open connections on demand, as the new instances took traffic; request volume was normal, so a traffic spike doesn't explain it.\n\n**Fix, verified in the sandbox:** restore the default pool size to 20, and add a test for the documented rule `DB_POOL_SIZE × INSTANCES ≤ max_connections`. The new test fails on v1.4.8, and the whole suite passes with the fix.",
