      "title": "Restore DB_POOL_SIZE to 20 so 5 instances fit max_connections",
      "body": "## What happened\nSince v1.4.8 (6 Oct, 14:20), `POST /payments` fails with 500: `OperationalError: too many connections` on all 5 instances, 94 failed payments in the first hour.\n\n## Why\nCommit 5b0bb55c90 raised the default `DB_POOL_SIZE` from 20 to 100. Each instance keeps its own pool, so 5 × 100 = 500 connections against Postgres `max_connections` of 100. `docs/database.md` requires `DB_POOL_SIZE × INSTANCES ≤ max_connections`, and INC-017 was the same failure with a pool of 60.\n\n## Change\n- `src/paystream/database/config.py`: default `DB_POOL_SIZE` back to 20 (5 × 20 = 100).\n- `tests/test_pool_fits_database.py`: a test for the documented rule, so a pool change that breaks it fails CI.\n\n## Verified\n- The new test fails on v1.4.8 (baseline), as expected.\n- The whole suite passes with the fix (15 passed).\n\nInvestigated by RootTrace AI."
    }
